  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The analysis relies on a structural matrix-based modeling approach (MICMAC) to map variables, which is inherently dependent on the subjective ranking and selection of the thirteen input variables.",
      "what": "This study analyzes the interrelations and indirect influences of thirteen strategic variables across political, economic, social, technological, legal, and environmental domains shaping the trucking industry's trajectory toward 2030. Using cross-impact matrix multiplication applied to a ranking (MICMAC) analysis, it evaluates how drivers like digitalization, artificial intelligence, and policy shifts impact industry outcomes.",
      "why": "It establishes that technological adoption (digitalization and AI) will be the primary driver of change, while company economics will remain the most dependent variable and the influence of policy is projected to decrease by 2030."
    }
